      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While diet and stress management are crucial, relying solely on vitamins might not address the root cause of these sudden episodes. Dehydration and blood sugar dips from skipping meals combined with too much caffeine can definitely mimic cognitive confusion. Instead of immediately starting supplements, try consistent hydration and eating balanced, regular meals first. If these changes don't help, please consider local low-cost clinics or telehealth options for an initial consultation.",
      "source": "target",
